  "notes": "{移民|いみん} means both the person (immigrant/emigrant) and the act (immigration/emigration). It can be used with する as a verb.\n\nWORD FORMATION:\n{移|い} (move) + {民|みん} (people)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {移民|いみん}{政策|せいさく}: immigration policy\n- {移民|いみん}ビザ: immigration visa\n- {不法|ふほう}{移民|いみん}: illegal immigrant\n- {移民|いみん}を{受|う}け{入|い}れる: to accept immigrants\n- 〜に{移民|いみん}する: to immigrate to ~\n\nDISTINCTION:\n- {移民|いみん}: immigrant (voluntary relocation)\n- {難民|なんみん}: refugee (forced displacement)\n- {帰化|きか}: naturalization (becoming a citizen)\n\nHISTORICAL NOTE:\nJapan has a history of {移民|いみん} to Brazil, Hawaii, and the Americas in the late 19th and early 20th centuries.",
